{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries","id":1211201,"title":"Questions on Phylacteries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-24T16:09:49-07:00","id":1211201,"title":"Questions on Phylacteries","content":"- Without a Phylactery you are a Sleeper. Does this mean you act as a Sleeper Witness without it?<br /> <br /> - If a Mage character with a Phylactery loses their body, can they reasonably expect to eek out an existence possessing cultists / retainers / the comatose / clones? I mean in a sense of difficulty, and the power level required to do so reliably.<br /> <br /> - Can a Phylactery exist in its own right? Traditionally in MtA they are created by investing the Avatar of a Mage inside of a certain item, along with some of their essence and part of their mind. They are bound to it. But could Magick craft an object which simply holds an accessible Avatar? A Mjolnir-like object where &quot;worthy&quot; (naturally depending on the avatar; gods help the fool who is deemed worthy of a fallen avatar) individuals who hold it may act as Mages for as long as they possess it. The object might have a bloodied history being pursued by occultists and sorcerers and Mages for its power. Such an Avatar could act as an antagonist. How many proxies does the Evil Belt of Doom need to go through before we figure out that it is the mastermind of unfolding events?<br /> <br /> - Can a Mage have multiple Phylacteries? Perhaps 7 of them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=buJPwD5nW1g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=buJPwD5nW1g</a>). So each Phylactery would hold a portion of the Mage's Avatar, would be the idea. My gut instinct is that this falls into the realm of Archspheres, but I'm curious.<br /> <br /> - If a Mage's Phylactery is destroyed, they lose the ability to use magick. However, Avatars reincarnate. If they got lucky and their Avatar returned to the mortal plane within their lifetime, would they still be connected to it? Would they be able to recover it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T17:23:21-07:00","id":1211231,"title":"","content":"I think they would be like a sorcerer in terms of counting as a witness, as in they wouldn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Depends on what spheres they have, and what enchantments they had placed on their phylactert. Nothing\u2019s comes to the unprepared.<br /> <br /> Sure, but I imagine it would require being a master of both Spirit and Prime, and may be really messy to pull off.<br /> <br /> If you cut your avatar in half, I don\u2019t think that\u2019s going to do much for your ability to perform magic. Also you\u2019d probably need to carry them all around with you to be able to do anything unimpeded. So I file this under \u201cpossible but ill advised\u201d.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say the avatar would reincarnate in a new born baby if it returned to the mortal plane. In theory it would certainly be possible with the right spheres to conduct a modified gilgul rite to pull it out and return it to yourself... but how exactly are you going to do that? You\u2019d need outside help for such a feat as magic is now beyond you, and that essentially means finding people willing to help you and capable of doing it. And the chances are such a service will not come cheap.<br /> Also, how are you going to know it\u2019s your avatar? And what chance do you even have of finding it? For all you know they are going to reincarnate 12 years from now inside a baby born at the southern tip of Chile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T06:20:56-07:00","id":1211386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Can a Mage have multiple Phylacteries? Perhaps 7 of them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=buJPwD5nW1g\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=buJPwD5nW1g</a>). So each Phylactery would hold a portion of the Mage's Avatar, would be the idea. My gut instinct is that this falls into the realm of Archspheres, but I'm curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's a...Merit?...that implies your avatar it's cut in pieces and that you can rejoin the pieces to get a higher Avatar rating (supposedly one of the few ways to increase one's Avatar after char gen).<br /> <br /> So I would use that Merit as a template for that. I think that Spirit 5, being enough to shatter an avatar should be enough to cut a piece of it. Add Prime 5, maybe Entropy 5, to manipulate the conceptual &quot;self&quot; of that shard and place it into the thing. Don't Botch.<br /> <br /> However, the merit implies your mage wants to join his pieces back together. So there isn't a mechanical benefit into making a horcrux...unless you are a Nephandi, or other horrid criminal that was discovered and can expect to be busted and Gilguled. Then cutting part of your Avatar and putting it into something may allow to regain your magick after the fact (though you still need to arrange your survival / resurrection).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:34:45-07:00","id":1211482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211386#post1211386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, there's a...Merit?...that implies your avatar it's cut in pieces and that you can rejoin the pieces to get a higher Avatar rating (supposedly one of the few ways to increase one's Avatar after char gen).<br /> <br /> So I would use that Merit as a template for that. I think that Spirit 5, being enough to shatter an avatar should be enough to cut a piece of it. Add Prime 5, maybe Entropy 5, to manipulate the conceptual &quot;self&quot; of that shard and place it into the thing. Don't Botch.<br /> <br /> However, the merit implies your mage wants to join his pieces back together. So there isn't a mechanical benefit into making a horcrux...unless you are a Nephandi, or other horrid criminal that was discovered and can expect to be busted and Gilguled. Then cutting part of your Avatar and putting it into something may allow to regain your magick after the fact (though you still need to arrange your survival / resurrection).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the Shattered Avatar Merit (?) is such a piss-poor idea.<br /> <br /> &quot;You get Avatar 1, and there are 4 pieces of Avatar our there you can claim.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, okay. How much will that cost me?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;5 freebies.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Couldn't I just... take 5 dots in Avatar? For 5 freebies total? Rather than spend 6 freebies to have, essentially, 1 dot in Avatar.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T11:39:44-07:00","id":1211486,"title":"","content":"I swear that should be a flaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T12:15:08-07:00","id":1211498,"title":"","content":"I could see it as a Merit if you had to pay 1pt instead of 5. As 5pt Merit it's nonsense.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of being a highlander-like character chasing for Avatar pieces, and certainly increasing Avatar to potentially 5 it's good if you have it at low levels. But since you have to spend 5 pts on the &quot;Merit&quot;, it's worse than useless. And now you may have people hunting your Avatar-shard. That's so not a Merit<br /> <br /> Before BoS it was often theorized than that Merit was the only way to get your Avatar rating above 5 (the clause saying that it can only increase up to 5 it's new). That's still of dubious use (because there's limits to what you can get spending Quint), but was better than the new version.<br /> <br /> Still, as a post char-gen action, I think that's how a shattered but still functional avatar should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:02:23-07:00","id":1211518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211498#post1211498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before BoS it was often theorized than that Merit was the only way to get your Avatar rating above 5 (the clause saying that it can only increase up to 5 it's new). That's still of dubious use (because there's limits to what you can get spending Quint), but was better than the new version.</div> </div> </div> </div>^ That, pretty much. It made total sense as an expensive merit, if it was a story hook to be able to get your avatar above 5. Without that giving you an advantage - you know, a character MERIT - it is useless as written right now. I'd ignore the Avatar 5 limit on it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:26:53-07:00","id":1211535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211486#post1211486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I swear that should be a flaw.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly agreed. It could easily be rejigged as one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T13:29:24-07:00","id":1211536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211498#post1211498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it as a Merit if you had to pay 1pt instead of 5. As 5pt Merit it's nonsense.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of being a highlander-like character chasing for Avatar pieces, and certainly increasing Avatar to potentially 5 it's good if you have it at low levels. But since you have to spend 5 pts on the &quot;Merit&quot;, it's worse than useless. And now you may have people hunting your Avatar-shard. That's so not a Merit<br /> <br /> Before BoS it was often theorized than that Merit was the only way to get your Avatar rating above 5 (the clause saying that it can only increase up to 5 it's new). That's still of dubious use (because there's limits to what you can get spending Quint), but was better than the new version.<br /> <br /> Still, as a post char-gen action, I think that's how a shattered but still functional avatar should work.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only spend 3 Quintessence on a spell normally, yes (with the exception of a case where the difficulty is hiked up, meaning that it takes more than 3 to get to the -3 difficulty maximum), but Avatar is still very useful.<br /> <br /> The Quint linked to your Avatar rating is safe. It can't be removed with Magick, short of directly attacking your pattern. It 100% belongs to you. Furthermore, the more powerful your Avatar is, the greater the vicious drive that pushes you to Seek and learn and grow. This is a story point, but important. An Avatar at 6+ would make you seem powerful, even if you weren't all that powerful, to someone with Spirit and Prime.<br /> <br /> And as a very minor point, Gilgul needs successes equal to your Arete + Avatar + Willpower, so raising your Avatar above 5 could be useful in that very specific scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T14:58:13-07:00","id":1211577,"title":"","content":"Shattered avatar merit is not powerful in the &quot;catch them all fragments&quot; part.<br /> it is powerful when you find the fragments in sleepers, you awaken them, and then you are linked to them at soul level.<br /> Which means you are a perfect team if you work with them. You can split the learning of the sphere between you, and once one has mind 4, everyone will be synchronized.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T15:02:08-07:00","id":1211579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RandyRando</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211577#post1211577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shattered avatar merit is not powerful in the &quot;catch them all fragments&quot; part.<br /> it is powerful when you find the fragments in sleepers, you awaken them, and then you are linked to them at soul level.<br /> Which means you are a perfect team if you work with them. You can split the learning of the sphere between you, and once one has mind 4, everyone will be synchronized.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That falls outside of the limits of the merit however. Twin Souls gives the sort of effect you're talking about.<br /> <br /> Shattered Avatar has a very &quot;there can only be one&quot; vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T15:13:11-07:00","id":1211584,"title":"","content":"Ho . I thought there were the same merit. Thats so sad and useless then..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T18:06:11-07:00","id":1212088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211482#post1211482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah the Shattered Avatar Merit (?) is such a piss-poor idea.<br /> <br /> &quot;You get Avatar 1, and there are 4 pieces of Avatar our there you can claim.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, okay. How much will that cost me?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;5 freebies.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Couldn't I just... take 5 dots in Avatar? For 5 freebies total? Rather than spend 6 freebies to have, essentially, 1 dot in Avatar.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Shattered avatar allows you to potentially have an avatar of more than 5 dots. That's why it is so costly. Now what KIND of avatar that is, I have no idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12911,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","user":"Lateral.Psychotropy","date":".  spelling 04-26-2018, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T22:12:45-07:00","id":1212154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1211536#post1211536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can only spend 3 Quintessence on a spell normally, yes (with the exception of a case where the difficulty is hiked up, meaning that it takes more than 3 to get to the -3 difficulty maximum),</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought so until recently, too, but you actually, literally can only spend 3 Quint total to reduce difficulty, even if the difficulty is above base :|<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lateral.Psychotropy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212088#post1212088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shattered avatar allows you to potentially have an avatar of more than 5 dots. That's why it is so costly. Now what KIND of avatar that is, I have no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in M20. It is limited to getting a max of 5 *after* collecting all the shards. Which is why it doesn't make sense as a merit in that edition, given that it costs as much as getting Avatar 5 in the first place. It should either be a flaw (And require Avatar 1), OR that limitation should be dropped. Quote from the Book Of Secrets:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No matter how many<br /> pieces are involved, however, the<br /> Avatar Background maxes out at<br /> 5 dots. Although this Merit allows you to<br /> raise your Trait\u2019s rating, it does not allow<br /> you to raise it above that level. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-27-2018, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:20:15-07:00","id":1212210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212154#post1212154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought so until recently, too, but you actually, literally can only spend 3 Quint total to reduce difficulty, even if the difficulty is above base :|</div> </div> </div> </div>Was that changed from Revised? Because the way I remember it working was as much Quintessence as Avatar could be used to reduce difficulty of a roll, but the max negative modifier overall could on be -3 from base difficulty.<br /> <br /> This means, if you had enough Quintessence, and a high avatar, you could pump in 5 points, lower it to -3 and keep it there until other things raised beyond a few points.<br /> <br /> Example, base diff is 7, you pump five points in to make it 4. You fail the roll, it stays at 4, you fail again, it\u2019s still at 4, you fail a third time, and now it goes up to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:22:58-07:00","id":1212214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212210#post1212210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was that changed from Revised? Because the way I remember it working was as much Quintessence as Avatar could be used to reduce difficulty of a roll, but the max negative modifier overall could on be -3 from base difficulty.<br /> <br /> This means, if you had enough Quintessence, and a high avatar, you could pump in 5 points, lower it to -3 and keep it there until other things raised beyond a few points.<br /> <br /> Example, base diff is 7, you pump five points in to make it 4. You fail the roll, it stays at 4, you fail again, it\u2019s still at 4, you fail a third time, and now it goes up to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>The example I thought of was working with raised difficulties.<br /> <br /> Say you are Fast-Casting without a Focus. That's +2 difficulty (I think).<br /> <br /> If you have Avatar 5 you can spend 5 points of Quintessence to reduce the difficulty to -3, compared with the base difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T04:24:45-07:00","id":1212217,"title":"","content":"@11twiggins<br /> That\u2019s pretty much the same thing as far as numbers go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:51:04-07:00","id":1212275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212210#post1212210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was that changed from Revised? Because the way I remember it working was as much Quintessence as Avatar could be used to reduce difficulty of a roll, but the max negative modifier overall could on be -3 from base difficulty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. I just checked the Revised Magical Difficulty Table, and both the M20 and the Revised table state that you can only use Quintessence to give a -3 reduction max.<br /> Ths is easily confusable with the Maximum -3 modifier from *base* difficulty because of the same number, but sadly does not refer to the same thing. As I said, I was pretty much sure that they both meant the same thing myself, until recent re-reading.<br /> <br /> Simply put, If the *base* coincidence/vulgarity difficulty of a spell is 6, but circumstances drive that to 9 (Like time turning backward), using Quintessence alone you only can push it back down to 6.<br /> Both books also state explicitely in the Quintessence section that a max of 3 points can be spent on this, so it's double-verified.<br /> <br /> Personally I *would* houserule it so that you can spend as much as your Avatar rating allows (with the max -3 from base modifier in mind), but it's not a RAW.<br /> But in my opinion, that houserule would also give more mechanical incentive to get Avatar 4/5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-27-2018, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:59:44-07:00","id":1212279,"title":"","content":"Related feature; the Nephilim / Laham merit makes it so that every day you wake up with 7 points of Quintessence, charged and ready to go. This ignores your Avatar rating essentially, since it states a 7-point maximum and says that its behaviour isn't affected by the Avatar rating. So the merit means that having an Avatar of 3 is ideal really. The 2 points you save here could be spent on Advantages (say hello to my demi-god, son of thor, he's pretty bad at magick (not the brightest) but he has giant raven's wings and wolverine's healing factor, plus Aggravated claws).<br /> <br /> Add some Prime, and store your daily dose of Quintessence from your half-angel/demon/god/eldritch nature through some method. Charge up a Wonder, fill a Soulgem... and then when you really need it you can fill up your wheel with Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 04-27-2018, 11:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:52:56-07:00","id":1212308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212275#post1212275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. I just checked the Revised Magical Difficulty Table, and both the M20 and the Revised table state that you can only use Quintessence to give a -3 reduction max.<br /> Ths is easily confusable with the Maximum -3 modifier from *base* difficulty because of the same number, but sadly does not refer to the same thing. As I said, I was pretty much sure that they both meant the same thing myself, until recent re-reading.<br /> <br /> Simply put, If the *base* coincidence/vulgarity difficulty of a spell is 6, but circumstances drive that to 9 (Like time turning backward), using Quintessence alone you only can push it back down to 6.<br /> Both books also state explicitely in the Quintessence section that a max of 3 points can be spent on this, so it's double-verified.<br /> <br /> Personally I *would* houserule it so that you can spend as much as your Avatar rating allows (with the max -3 from base modifier in mind), but it's not a RAW.<br /> But in my opinion, that houserule would also give more mechanical incentive to get Avatar 4/5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those examples are actually referring to net changes from the base difficulty. You can spend more than 3 Quintessence to reduce difficulty - you just can't deviate more than 3 points from the base. See the example on M20, page 537 under &quot;Adjusting Arete Rolls&quot; for an example of spending 5 Quintessence. Revised says the same (p 149), where it makes clear that you're actually limited by your Avatar rating or a net total of 3. The texts generally explain it in more detail than the tables <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:05:23-07:00","id":1212314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212308#post1212308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those examples are actually referring to net changes from the base difficulty. You can spend more than 3 Quintessence to reduce difficulty - you just can't deviate more than 3 points from the base. See the example on M20, page 537 under &quot;Adjusting Arete Rolls&quot; for an example of spending 5 Quintessence. Revised says the same (p 149), where it makes clear that you're actually limited by your Avatar rating or a net total of 3. The texts generally explain it in more detail than the tables <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>...I seeeeeriously wish the books would not constantly contradict themselves (Or rather would be written with more clear wording)!<br /> Both book's Quintessence sections (not the table) either mention that only 3 points can be spent and/or the reduction can only be a max of -3 through Quintessence alone. But I guess the explicit examples on the pages you mention make it clear that this, after all, refers to the net difficulty modifier.<br /> <br /> But, hooray! That means that the rule I prefer is actually RAW, and I read it right the first time before my recent 'let down' :P Thank you for clearing that up!<br /> <br /> Giggidy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 04-27-2018, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T09:11:25-07:00","id":1212318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212314#post1212314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...I seeeeeriously wish the books would not constantly contradict themselves (Or rather would be written with more clear wording)!</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis is Mage. Cease your crazy talk.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212314#post1212314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, hooray! That means that the rule I prefer is actually RAW, and I read it right the first time before my recent 'let down' :P Thank you for clearing that up!<br /> <br /> Giggidy.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> No worries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2543-thebian","name":"Thebian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2543_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T10:48:44-07:00","id":1212357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thebian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212318#post1212318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No worries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to have it cleared up! In VtM you only have a few degrees of rules comprehension, while Mage seems to have manifold intricacies...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T11:06:01-07:00","id":1212365,"title":"","content":"We've all been there, in the quiet summoned by rule paradox.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T13:02:34-07:00","id":1212398,"title":"","content":"On the bright side, it\u2019s stuff like this which makes rule lawyering impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T14:21:25-07:00","id":1212421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212398#post1212398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the bright side, it\u2019s stuff like this which makes rule lawyering impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Great video on the topic of &quot;Rule Law&quot; that's worth watching. Uses DnD examples, but it's all applicable to WoD games.<br /> <br /> He essentially draws a line between being a &quot;Rules Traditionalist&quot; (believes that the game is fun because of the mechanics, thinks following the rules well will lead to a good experience, applies the rules evenly generally speaking, helpful player who knows the rules) and being a &quot;Rules Haggler&quot; (all they want is to get the result they're looking for, and the rules are a tool to achieve that; they'll happily ignore the rules when they don't work in their favour, but will happily jump in with rules that benefit them when the moment arises).<br /> <br /> Not 100% relevant but worth watching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T01:51:12-07:00","id":1212567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212421#post1212421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=wnj0CDX096A </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Great video on the topic of &amp;quot;Rule Law&amp;quot; that's worth watching. Uses DnD examples, but it's all applicable to WoD games.<br /> <br /> He essentially draws a line between being a &amp;quot;Rules Traditionalist&amp;quot; (believes that the game is fun because of the mechanics, thinks following the rules well will lead to a good experience, applies the rules evenly generally speaking, helpful player who knows the rules) and being a &amp;quot;Rules Haggler&amp;quot; (all they want is to get the result they're looking for, and the rules are a tool to achieve that; they'll happily ignore the rules when they don't work in their favour, but will happily jump in with rules that benefit them when the moment arises).<br /> <br /> Not 100% relevant but worth watching.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve seen it, and I\u2019m not convinced either variant is really able to function in Mage. The nature of paradigm requires exceptions to certain rules or addition of extra rules depending on the specifics of the mage\u2019s beliefs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T02:46:30-07:00","id":1212573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212567#post1212567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve seen it, and I\u2019m not convinced either variant is really able to function in Mage. The nature of paradigm requires exceptions to certain rules or addition of extra rules depending on the specifics of the mage\u2019s beliefs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure? M20 has a lot of rules which relate to certain paradigms having fundamentally different beliefs, and while many of these are optional rules, I think there is room for these two concepts within the game.<br /> <br /> For example, a Rules Traditionalist might point out that the Chorister PC's healing effect should be at -1 difficulty, since they're using the right kind of resonance, for example their Tass might be The Oil of the Sick. Or they might point out that a Mage (themselves, or another PC) is fast-casting and should be at +1 difficulty.<br /> <br /> A Rules Haggler will ask for exceptions, and conveniently forget certain downsides. For example, they'll never remind the ST about their points of Permanent Paradox if the ST forgets, they'll argue that something is Coincidental when it clearly falls outside of the Consensus (and even they know that), and they'll push for things which directly contradict the rules like starting with more than 2 points of Do or using unfamiliar Hypertech with less than Hypertech 3.<br /> <br /> The essential distinction is Good Faith vs. Bad Faith, and I think that applies to any tabletop system. And a player might just forget their negative modifiers, and forget to note down their Paradox, people make mistakes. The problem comes when it forms a pattern, and it becomes clear that someone isn't haggling in good faith. The player who moans when others get away with something dubious, but constantly fights their own corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:50:34-07:00","id":1212616,"title":"","content":"Good thing with mage is that in theory, paradox can come out without reason, and players which refuse to be in tune with the game rules consensus can see their character in strange situations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","user":"RandyRando","date":". 04-28-2018, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T15:44:46-07:00","id":1212820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1212573#post1212573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure? M20 has a lot of rules which relate to certain paradigms having fundamentally different beliefs, and while many of these are optional rules, I think there is room for these two concepts within the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically I can see (related to that video link) a Rules Haggler to be more at home in Mage than a Rules Traditionalist. Especially given that Mage is all about the paradigms and them explaining certain exceptions or changes to the standard rules.<br /> <br /> A Rules Traditionalist would push their thumb onto using, for example, HDYDT as written...and that alone would probably run contrary to many people here on the forums alone.<br /> <br /> Heck, the main redeeming quality of the book itself is that it pretty much states 'If you do not like some or any of the rules in this book, feel free to drop them and use your own'. Which shows, all in all, quite a healthy anount of self-awareness on the side of Phil regarding the book, which I highly respect. But it runs right-on contradictionary to that Rules Traditionalist as depicted. As do many other parts of Mage where exceptions are made, circumstances dictate the exact way to go about things, and the fluid nature of reality is reflected in the rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T01:02:02-07:00","id":1213353,"title":"","content":"I know this was unintended, but a love the term \u2018contradictionary\u2019<br /> <br /> It perfectly describes HDYDT.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T04:34:39-07:00","id":1213375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1213353#post1213353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this was unintended, but a love the term \u2018contradictionary\u2019<br /> <br /> It perfectly describes HDYDT.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really get people's problem with the Spheres in M20.<br /> <br /> Previous editions had a tonne of pages devoted to Rotes, which were full of contradictory ideas and rules. M20 just uses a simple table which covers most of the effects that come up (a simple entry in a table for &quot;Physical Illusions&quot; covers ground that you might cover in 4 rotes), and has HDYDT? for complex stuff.<br /> <br /> Granted, HDYDT does have a few problems, but these problems, IMO, are the exception to the rule. People talk about the Chi Healing and the Chi Shields as examples of &quot;do the same thing, but Worse!&quot; mechanics, which to be fair were poor writing, but they don't talk about all of the stuff that works, like the rules on binding and summoning and warding, which are comprehensive, clear and concise. And I would argue that the latter is the general experience, and the weird and pointless mechanics are more rare.<br /> <br /> Honestly I just wish that M20's books had all had purely digital releases. I know people love the physical books, but it would be good if they could just Errata stuff to deal with contradictions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T05:25:57-07:00","id":1213384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1213375#post1213375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, HDYDT does have a few problems, but these problems, IMO, are the exception to the rule. People talk about the Chi Healing and the Chi Shields as examples of &quot;do the same thing, but Worse!&quot; mechanics, which to be fair were poor writing, but they don't talk about all of the stuff that works, like the rules on binding and summoning and warding, which are comprehensive, clear and concise. And I would argue that the latter is the general experience, and the weird and pointless mechanics are more rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind you, I don't dislike HDYDT. I got the print edition sitting right on my shelf. But it is definitely a book that pretty much everybody cherry-picks from as far as I have seen and read, according to personal preference.<br /> This does not make it a *bad* book, but given that Mage had the people come up with explanations and, shall we say, recipes for effects for almost 20 years, a lot of stuff contained in it will clash with what other people have come up with. Again - not a bad thing, and the disclaimer at the front makes it kind of self-aware about the issue - but that's the reason it literally is handled like a 'Book of effect house rules' a lot.<br /> Now, to a group new to Mage? They can snatch up a lot more from its contents without plucking it apart according to previous established things. That still leaves the sheer sphere bloat for some things you mentioned, but c'est la vie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T05:43:27-07:00","id":1213387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1213384#post1213384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, I don't dislike HDYDT. I got the print edition sitting right on my shelf. But it is definitely a book that pretty much everybody cherry-picks from as far as I have seen and read, according to personal preference.<br /> This does not make it a *bad* book, but given that Mage had the people come up with explanations and, shall we say, recipes for effects for almost 20 years, a lot of stuff contained in it will clash with what other people have come up with. Again - not a bad thing, and the disclaimer at the front makes it kind of self-aware about the issue - but that's the reason it literally is handled like a 'Book of effect house rules' a lot.<br /> Now, to a group new to Mage? They can snatch up a lot more from its contents without plucking it apart according to previous established things. That still leaves the sheer sphere bloat for some things you mentioned, but c'est la vie.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't care if something in M20 contradicts the past, on principle at least. It's a new edition, and it will change mechanics and ret-con lore. The SoE have a recipe for Primium? Not in M20, unless you would prefer to keep the Revised stance on it of course. Golden Rule applies naturally.<br /> <br /> So if the Sphere effects aren't exactly the same as the past, I don't really get why someone would complain about that without explaining why the change is bad on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> As for the cherry-picking, I feel like &quot;this is different&quot; are the worst cases, &quot;this contradicts something else in M20&quot; is better, and &quot;this is pointless, objectively inferior to another option, or adds nothing&quot;, which are good criticism.<br /> <br /> For example, there are a lot of things in HDYDT which give you the same result, but demand that you spend Quintessence (as an optional rule, but still). The optional rule being presented is &quot;are you basing your paradigm around the flow of Chi/Ether/Mana? Well, now for the low low price of one precious point of Quintessence per effect, you can get the same magickal powers as everyone else!&quot;. If someone thinks that their Forcefield is a sphere of ether they are projecting from their living essence, then they should use the normal Spheres needed (Forces etc.), and only spend Quintessence if the effect they are using demands it (or if they want to reduce difficulty). Just my 2 cents, and I'm sure it has been said before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-01-2018, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T02:28:20-07:00","id":1214488,"title":"","content":"I FOUND A HUGE ADVANTAGE TO AVATAR!!!<br /> <br /> In M20, when a Spirit rolls to do damage, it rolls its Rage. A potent Water Incarna might have a Rage of 6 or higher, and each success inflicts a point of Lethal damage.<br /> <br /> Mages can actually soak this! They soak it with their Avatar rating. So with an Avatar of 5 against a Rage of 6, it's almost as though they had a Rage of 1 in terms of inflicting damage (on average).<br /> <br /> Now &quot;huge&quot; might be a push... it's definitely a huge advantage if you're working with, or against, spirits. I also feel like having a powerful Avatar will have an effect on some Spirits. If a Hermetic conjures up a powerful incarna, and is obviously a rank amateur, then it might just refuse to appear, or leave when it has had a second to deride (or punish) the Mage. But if it arrives and finds that the cheeky apprentice has a fierce, powerful Avatar, it might decide to do something else. Test them. Mentor them. Hurt them. To some spirits, holding a powerful Avatar might be a sign that a mortal is particularly blessed (or cursed) in a spiritual sense. Much as umbrood love Werewolves, some will respect Mages who have a potent spiritual aspect to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:31:44-07:00","id":1214569,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s automatic soak, I read it as giving you soak dice. And I remember in M20 that you could use ar\u00eate as additional soak if you had spirit 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T06:37:43-07:00","id":1214574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1214569#post1214569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s automatic soak, I read it as giving you soak dice. And I remember in M20 that you could use ar\u00eate as additional soak if you had spirit 1</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it forms a soak pool. My example was referring to the outcomes of rolls.<br /> <br /> So if their damage pool is 6, and your soak pool is 5, then on average (there's a lot of room for variation here) you are subtracting 5 dice from the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T14:32:31-07:00","id":1214775,"title":"","content":"Avatar with a rating of 5 .. aren't they demanding ?<br /> This is exactly how i could picture the relationship between a mage and her mysteries-hungry primordial avatar with a rating of 5 =&gt; <a href=\"http://mangakakalot.com/chapter/majin_tantei_nougami_neuro/chapter_1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mangakakalot.com/chapter/maji...euro/chapter_1</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23946-randyrando","name":"RandyRando","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23946_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T20:05:04-07:00","id":1214887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RandyRando</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1214775#post1214775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Avatar with a rating of 5 .. aren't they demanding ?<br /> This is exactly how i could picture the relationship between a mage and her mysteries-hungry primordial avatar with a rating of 5 =&gt; <a href=\"http://mangakakalot.com/chapter/majin_tantei_nougami_neuro/chapter_1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mangakakalot.com/chapter/maji...euro/chapter_1</a></div> </div> </div> </div>(Ah, I see you are also a man of great taste. It's been so long since I read this series.)<br /> <br /> I can totally see Neuro being a very demanding Avatar to a poor young Mage like Yako. Driving her to solve Enigmas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:42:32-07:00","id":1215076,"title":"","content":"Once Avatars are more than Quintessential batteries and become characters the real potential of an Avatar rating of 4-5 manifests. Such Avatar it's a powerful being on it's own right and may reward you if you follow it's agenda (just as he can fuck you if you don't).<br /> <br /> For instance, one could argue that if you haven't Avatar related Backgrounds with such a potent Avatar, it may very well be because the Avatar ain't sharing them with you. With the ST blessing, this opens the potential to buy things like Past Lives or Dreams after character gen (within a suitable story involving your Avatar tormen...erm...teaching your character, of course <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> Such an avatar SHOULD be a potent asset, just as it drives you kicking &amp; screaming towards enligthenment (and madness, but who needs sanity when you have magic(k)?). Who knows what such a potent Avatar can do or teach?. Spheres, lost Rotes, spiritual Merits (and Defects) - all are fair game 'cause the Avatar it's magic(k) and knows better.<br /> <br /> Buuut that enters in the lofty realm of ST discretion. Then again, so does interpreting a &quot;demanding&quot; Avatar.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd there's always the C<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">ircumspect </span></span>Avatar Merit for those that just don't want to deal with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T09:35:36-07:00","id":1215109,"title":"","content":"Circumspect Avatar puts up a reference how much of a hassle an Avatar should be. If it were the other way round, having an Avatar interfering with your stuff would be a 3 point flaw...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T03:02:32-07:00","id":1215423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215109#post1215109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Circumspect Avatar puts up a reference how much of a hassle an Avatar should be. If it were the other way round, having an Avatar interfering with your stuff would be a 3 point flaw...</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocrats seem to have this by default though. Making it a merit is so weird. Their &quot;Genius&quot; doesn't tend to bother them much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T03:46:52-07:00","id":1215434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215423#post1215423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technocrats seem to have this by default though. Making it a merit is so weird. Their &quot;Genius&quot; doesn't tend to bother them much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their genius bothers them a great deal, they are just a lot better at hiding it.<br /> <br /> It might be a phone call, a man in a black suit, secret messages delivered via carrier pigeon, flashes of insight, a series of beeps, a guy at the bar, or just a killer instinct, but it\u2019s always there lurking in the corner.<br /> <br /> Some might even have more mystical \u201cgenius\u201d, perhaps a guardian angel, the ghost of their long dead husband, Father Time, Luna, or even, as contrary as it may seem, a fairy.<br /> <br /> These technocrats would probably have a hell of a task trying to hide this avatar, and may even find ways of rationalising it or just think they must be schizophrenic and take progenitor medication to block it out, or at least keep it sanitised.<br /> <br /> Or maybe not, maybe there\u2019s a syndicate member at the top of their game who regularly converses with a skull they keep in their cabinet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-05-2018, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-05T07:13:23-07:00","id":1215475,"title":"","content":"For many Technocrats, their &quot;Genius&quot; is a topic politely avoided, when they consider it at all. No one wants to be labeled Unmutual, and talking about supernatural beings that talk to them on occasion is the quickest way to get the third degree, and maybe a trip to Room 101. So every Technocrat with an overactive Eidolon will keep it to themselves, as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Many of them also get VERY good at rationalizing. If an operative experiences vivid dreams, where an abstract or seemingly mythic figure gives them information or riddles, they're more likely to chalk the experience up to stress. Or else tell themselves that it's just their subconscious constructing symbolic frameworks, in order to process and relay information the operative picked up on but hasn't comprehended on a conscious level yet.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, also, that Avatars tend to interact with their mages in a manner that matches the character's Paradigm, attitudes, and personal needs. A Technocrat's Eidolon might react to their charge's refusal to acknowledge it as a part of himself, and play along. If the Technocrat thinks the Avatar is a foreign entity or a malignant suppressed aspect of his psyche - or even an internalized construct embodying his hatred for filthy superstitionists - the Avatar will acquiesce to this assumption. In this case, the Avatar's relationship with the Technocrat is adversarial, challenging him like some sort of great enemy. All while having the challenges be shaped by what the mage needs to further their path towards Ascension. Even if that means the Avatar needs to use reverse psychology. If the Technocrat sees his internal enemy seemingly wants him to zig, he'll zag just to spite it, not knowing until later that zagging is exactly what the Avatar wanted him to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T09:15:17-07:00","id":1215821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215475#post1215475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For many Technocrats, their &quot;Genius&quot; is a topic politely avoided, when they consider it at all. No one wants to be labeled Unmutual, and talking about supernatural beings that talk to them on occasion is the quickest way to get the third degree, and maybe a trip to Room 101. So every Technocrat with an overactive Eidolon will keep it to themselves, as much as possible.<br /> <br /> Many of them also get VERY good at rationalizing. If an operative experiences vivid dreams, where an abstract or seemingly mythic figure gives them information or riddles, they're more likely to chalk the experience up to stress. Or else tell themselves that it's just their subconscious constructing symbolic frameworks, in order to process and relay information the operative picked up on but hasn't comprehended on a conscious level yet.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, also, that Avatars tend to interact with their mages in a manner that matches the character's Paradigm, attitudes, and personal needs. A Technocrat's Eidolon might react to their charge's refusal to acknowledge it as a part of himself, and play along. If the Technocrat thinks the Avatar is a foreign entity or a malignant suppressed aspect of his psyche - or even an internalized construct embodying his hatred for filthy superstitionists - the Avatar will acquiesce to this assumption. In this case, the Avatar's relationship with the Technocrat is adversarial, challenging him like some sort of great enemy. All while having the challenges be shaped by what the mage needs to further their path towards Ascension. Even if that means the Avatar needs to use reverse psychology. If the Technocrat sees his internal enemy seemingly wants him to zig, he'll zag just to spite it, not knowing until later that zagging is exactly what the Avatar wanted him to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... in terms of the Mage / Avatar relationship, I wonder if an expertise in Spirit and Prime, perhaps with Mind, and a Paradigm which completely accepts Avatars as conscious and sentient beings with &quot;minds&quot; of their own, could allow a Mage to drive a wedge between a Mage and their Avatar, exploiting the fact that a Technocrat sees it as a malignant schizophrenic aspect of their mind, or some reality deviance that they have to keep quiet. Essentially they would be acting, mystically speaking, in concordance with what the Technocrat fears, and thinks they know.<br /> <br /> Acting as a psychiatric figure, breaking down metaphysical bonds (maybe some Entropy?) by hyping up the adversarial nature of this aspect of their psyche, by giving them medications which are meant to suppress it (a good coincidental focus), by using CBT which works to marginalize that aspect of their spiritual essence.<br /> <br /> As a dedicated villain, perhaps they could be a Negation Man who has decided (in their powerful denial) that they have discovered a rare and dangerous psychological affliction which seems to manifest with dangerous delusions of grandeur, paranormal mania and an intense belief in the impossible. As a former sufferer of this affliction they lure in those who have developed it and attempt to convert them to their way of thinking. The eventual aim of such would would be to generate a Denial backlash which leaves them as a Marauder. This would make the marauder in question unusual however, since despite their denial they would still be actively shaping reality (simply in a way which feeds denial and works against Avatars and Magick). Just some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-06-2018, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T14:01:22-07:00","id":1215890,"title":"","content":"If it was being done of purpose, that kind of thing seems like it would only really be functional with the qlippothic spheres. These are the spheres the nephandi use, and require an inverted avatar to even attempt. I\u2019d say qlippothic Spirit, Prime, and Mind would certainly be enough to sever ones psychic connection with their avatar, subbing in mind for Entropy would also work, but then the erosion would be an event that happens in time, rather than an effect you can directly influence.<br /> <br /> Your marauder may actually have a top level spot within the technocracy as we speak. My guess would be somewhere within the NWO. Around them, anything that was not strictly consensual magic would probably not work at all. They\u2019d be like the Haitian from hero\u2019s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T15:54:55-07:00","id":1215917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215890#post1215890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it was being done of purpose, that kind of thing seems like it would only really be functional with the qlippothic spheres. These are the spheres the nephandi use, and require an inverted avatar to even attempt. I\u2019d say qlippothic Spirit, Prime, and Mind would certainly be enough to sever ones psychic connection with their avatar, subbing in mind for Entropy would also work, but then the erosion would be an event that happens in time, rather than an effect you can directly influence.<br /> <br /> Your marauder may actually have a top level spot within the technocracy as we speak. My guess would be somewhere within the NWO. Around them, anything that was not strictly consensual magic would probably not work at all. They\u2019d be like the Haitian from hero\u2019s.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble is that the M20 mechanics have the Negation Men just turning everything off and having no choice in the matter. If they're present then their sheer disbelief, mechanically, means roll Arete and subtract successes from the Effect.<br /> <br /> With that said, the mechanics and fluff diverge a bit. I would change the mechanics to make it more flexible and allow for cool ideas like this, like high level Technocrats being Anti-Mages. So instead of casting their Arete against all effects, they only roll Arete against effects which are Vulgar, and they always count as a Witness. They are also stricter than the HAB. If it isn't strictly possible within consensual reality (as the Negation Man understands it) then it's Vulgar with Witnesses.<br /> <br /> If the inevitable Paradox backlash which occurs is bad enough to demand Quiet, then it will almost always be Denial around the Negator. So if the NWO had them in their ranks (I don't know if they do actually; M20 doesn't mention it but I wouldn't be shocked if it were in past books) then they would be dangerous but exceptionally useful.<br /> <br /> I did actually have an idea for a Nephandus Archmage whose evil plot was to create as many Negation Men as possible, and spread them like a plague through the world until magick died, destroying the soul of the universe at least a little bit each time. The idea is that they use psychological manipulation, Mind, Entropy and Spirit (for the psyche, the degradation of faith and manipulation of Paradox Spirits) to simply up the odds of Denial and becoming Mad. Once that is done, they use Mind rituals to control these Negators, relying on an insane number of successes to ignore their innate countermagick, and using them as pawns in a war on the Traditions and Technocracy.<br /> <br /> As for the Nephandi Spheres, I really love the idea of them being inversions of the Spheres related to their inverted Avatar, but I sometimes feel like the execution is a bit weird? It often feels like the normal Spheres are being shown with an evil snapchat filter. I read an example of a Nephandus tearing a hole in reality to get from one place to another, rather than simply opening a portal; the implication is that every time they use magick they are desecrating reality. But that sounds like something which will draw attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-06-2018, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T17:09:38-07:00","id":1215930,"title":"","content":"As stated in the revised book of madness, nephandi are perfectly capable of using the magic they had before they passed through the cauls, and in many cases they absolutely must in order to avoid detection.<br /> <br /> The qlippothic spheres function almost identically to the standard spheres though may leave a more bitter resonance, but then most great mages have all kinds of resonances so that alone won\u2019t be a great indicator.<br /> <br /> What truly sets the qlippothic spheres apart is that, by the sheer power of destruction, they can push beyond the limitations of the standard spheres.<br /> <br /> Q-Prime, for example, can rend the quintessence from ones avatar, draining a mage of quintessence entirely. While Prime cannot take the quintessence within the avatar by force.<br /> Q-Mind can ransack the targets mind of memories and identity and willpower, leaving them a hollow shell fit for any purpose the mage sees fit. While Mind is usually unable to completely remove all fragments of memory, even at mastery, as WillPower can still be used to attempt resistance.<br /> Q-corr. can, as you say, tear holes in the fabric of space while traveling between them, rendering the passage permanently forged, burnt into the very fabric of being. While standar Corr. Such a feat would only be possible with high ritual, and even then be simple to dispel.<br /> Other examples include Q-Spirit allowing nephandi to ignore the avatar storm entirely, or at least suffer marginal effects from it. As well as corrupt spirits towards their line of thinking (known to some as wyrm taint, known to others as just accepting reality).<br /> Q-Forces being able to counter and absorb any force based attacks by being their complete opposite, attacking primarily with void energy, stillness, and anti-heat, not just cold, but the inverse of heat itself.<br /> Q-Life can be used to absorb life from those nearby.<br /> Q-Matter can make fractals of complexity by breaking things down smaller and smaller, in much the way they build their labyrinths.<br /> Q-Time allowing for the complete removal of time within a localised area, trapping enemies into a perpetual \u201cnow\u201d.<br /> And Q-Entropy, of course, is ravenous undoing. Chance is destroyed, as is fate, as all things that were being built up simply disperse. They can cause all things to crumble around them, be it buildings, plans, or alliances. Hope itself can be destroyed through this sphere alone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 05-06-2018, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T17:25:38-07:00","id":1215933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215930#post1215930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As stated in the revised book of madness, nephandi are perfectly capable of using the magic they had before they passed through the cauls, and in many cases they absolutely must in order to avoid detection.<br /> <br /> The qlippothic spheres function almost identically to the standard spheres though may leave a more bitter resonance, but then most great mages have all kinds of resonances so that alone won\u2019t be a great indicator.<br /> <br /> What truly sets the qlippothic spheres apart is that, by the sheer power of destruction, they can push beyond the limitations of the standard spheres.<br /> <br /> Q-Prime, for example, can rend the quintessence from ones avatar, draining a mage of quintessence entirely. While Prime cannot take the quintessence within the avatar by force.<br /> Q-Mind can ransack the targets mind of memories and identity and willpower, leaving them a hollow shell fit for any purpose the mage sees fit. While Mind is usually unable to completely remove all fragments of memory, even at mastery, as WillPower can still be used to attempt resistance.<br /> Q-corr. can, as you say, tear holes in the fabric of space while traveling between them, rendering the passage permanently forged, burnt into the very fabric of being. While standar Corr. Such a feat would only be possible with high ritual, and even then be simple to dispel.<br /> Other examples include Q-Spirit allowing nephandi to ignore the avatar storm entirely, or at least suffer marginal effects from it. As well as corrupt spirits towards their line of thinking (known to some as wyrm taint, known to others as just accepting reality).<br /> Q-Forces being able to counter and absorb any force based attacks by being their complete opposite, attacking primarily with void energy, stillness, and anti-heat, not just cold, but the inverse of heat itself.<br /> Q-Life can be used to absorb life from those nearby.<br /> Q-Matter can make fractals of complexity by breaking things down smaller and smaller, in much the way they build their labyrinths.<br /> Q-Time allowing for the complete removal of time within a localised area, trapping enemies into a perpetual \u201cnow\u201d.<br /> And Q-Entropy, of course, is ravenous undoing. Chance is destroyed, as is fate, as all things that were being built up simply disperse. They can cause all things to crumble around them, be it buildings, plans, or alliances. Hope itself can be destroyed through this sphere alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow that's got a lot more bite than I expected. Permanent damage and removal is a great theme for them, so it's fitting.<br /> <br /> See I'm almost tempted... ;-)<br /> <br /> I will say that at some point I want to play an &quot;everything but fallen&quot; demonologist. Not an infernalist, he would point out immediately. Like any good Hermetic he does not beg spirits for their intervention (side-eye at Choristers, Verbena, Dreamers) or worship them, instead he commands them and sometimes bargains with them. Really play up the &quot;yeah we're the default wizards and everyone else is fine sure you can help if you like&quot; while remaining within what is considered polite. All about those subtle implications.<br /> <br /> The idea would be to mess around with &quot;dark forces&quot; (banes, demonic entities, malevolent spirits) without actually being Fallen, since that goes outside of PC bounds. Explore the limits of what is acceptable within the Traditions, and what a mage can handle. For example, does accepting a Bane inside of you and then subjugating it with Spirit to get Powers out of it actually harm you in a real sense? A quick route to power? A great way to stagnate your Arete? An effective method of attracting Garou? Let's find out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-06T18:18:15-07:00","id":1215947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215933#post1215933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh wow that's got a lot more bite than I expected. Permanent damage and removal is a great theme for them, so it's fitting.<br /> <br /> See I'm almost tempted... ;-)<br /> <br /> I will say that at some point I want to play an &quot;everything but fallen&quot; demonologist. Not an infernalist, he would point out immediately. Like any good Hermetic he does not beg spirits for their intervention (side-eye at Choristers, Verbena, Dreamers) or worship them, instead he commands them and sometimes bargains with them. Really play up the &quot;yeah we're the default wizards and everyone else is fine sure you can help if you like&quot; while remaining within what is considered polite. All about those subtle implications.<br /> <br /> The idea would be to mess around with &quot;dark forces&quot; (banes, demonic entities, malevolent spirits) without actually being Fallen, since that goes outside of PC bounds. Explore the limits of what is acceptable within the Traditions, and what a mage can handle. For example, does accepting a Bane inside of you and then subjugating it with Spirit to get Powers out of it actually harm you in a real sense? A quick route to power? A great way to stagnate your Arete? An effective method of attracting Garou? Let's find out!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Things that can only end well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-07T02:34:32-07:00","id":1216020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215947#post1215947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Things that can only end well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know right!!!<br /> <br /> High Council: Do you know why you're here?<br /> <br /> Hermetic: Hmm... does it have something to do with Sheabub the Great Deceive-<br /> <br /> High Council: Yes, it does have something to do with Sheabub the Great Deceiver.<br /> <br /> Hermetic: ... I mean he TOLD me that he had been trapped unjustly. And he promised he wouldn't hurt anyone.<br /> <br /> High Council: ...<br /> <br /> Hermetic: On reflection he may have lied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T00:31:55-07:00","id":1220457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1215933#post1215933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will say that at some point I want to play an &quot;everything but fallen&quot; demonologist.<br /> <br /> The idea would be to mess around with &quot;dark forces&quot; (banes, demonic entities, malevolent spirits) without actually being Fallen, since that goes outside of PC bounds. Explore the limits of what is acceptable within the Traditions, and what a mage can handle.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this character's standards, and this character concept, are based on looking at the actions and the decisions of the character and having the character ask himself or herself the question &quot;Does doing this make me as bad as the Nephandi ? &quot; and then following a reasoning of &quot;Not as bad as the Nephandi \u2013 thus I can do this.&quot; or \u201eAs bad as the Nephandi \u2013 thus this is a line I won\u2019t cross.\u201d , then I think that there is something terribly wrong with this way of reasoning and this concept ( and in-game, very possibly something is very wrong with this character ) ; and this has nothing to do with the character being a demonologist.<br /> I am not even sure if I can describe in exactly what way I think that this is horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> First, consider this - according to which method and logic the character would act in practice ?<br /> <br /> Is it 1) Would such a character avoid any actions ( within demonology and within other areas of interest ) that any Nephandus does ? If many Nephandi Mages decide in 2024 to focus on torturing specific social groups within human society in novel ways, does this character eschew these new methods of torturing mundane humans as an reprehensible action, to the point of not having any contact or arrangments with demons who might get attracted and grow more powerful due to existence of a new way of torturing that gives another definition of sadism and cruelty ?<br /> If it would be Technocrats, and not Nephandi, who would be doing this torturing, would this character associate himself with demons attracted to this style of torturing ?<br /> <br /> Or is it 2) Does the character avoid only those methods and actions that are directly linked to the Nephandi way of thinking, values and ideology ? Can such a distinction even be made in general about any Mage ( or any person ? ) ? After all, nearly everything that a Mage does relates to their values, ideology etc.<br /> I am at a loss here \u2013 how does this \u201eAnything it takes, power for the sake of power, knowledge at any cost \u2013 as long as it is not what the Nephandi do.\u201d character reasons and thinks within this way of thinking ? What are criteria of this Mage ? Could you describe the character a bit, and maybe also how did he or she come to this approach \u2013 was this Mage at some point personally involved with a Nephandus or many Nephandi, or does the character base his or her thinking on what Tradition Mages have told him or her about the Nephandi ? What does this Mage know about the Nephandi \u2013 from where did he or she get enough knowledge about the Nephandi to be able to base his or her actions on \u201enot being as bad as the Nephandi.\u201d .<br /> <br /> I honestly don\u2019t know which option \u2013 avoiding the very actions that the Nephandi do, or avoiding actions that might lead to thinking similarly to a Nephandus - is worse as a strict criterion to base one\u2019s actions. ( or a character concept as a player ) I guess you meant something in between, but I think this would be the worst option as a way of thinking for a character, somehow.<br /> <br /> [ Also - do you think there is enough information about the Nephandi in the World of Darkness books so that you can, at least roughly, draw borders that show the Nephandi's way of acting and how \u2018bad\u2019 they are ? I have doubts about this. I think it is very likely that such a character like you described would end up as someone saying &quot;Not as bad as the Nephandi.&quot; as empty words. ]<br /> <br /> <br /> Second - consider how persons in general decide what they will do and who they will be. I think that within most of frameworks of thinking in regards to this, it would be clear that the Nephandi's ( or any other group's ) way of acting is not the metric or the scale by which other persons should consider ( for example ) the validity and morality of their own actions. I think that the actions of a person, and their validity and morality, should be first and foremost looked at without a comparison with what other persons, or groups of persons, do.<br /> <br /> Also - the Nephandi are not the most \u2018evil\u2019 group in World of Darkness. Thus I think that - even when adopting this horrible ( in my opinion ) reasoning - it is an invalid deduction within it that a person can assuredly act in a better way and be a better person through very rigidly and strictly drawing borders with lines dictated by stopping short of &quot;not acting and not thinking like those Nephandi&quot; .<br /> <br /> <br /> Another factor to consider - the Nephandi might not do some actions, even though those actions would be very ( for example ) sadistic, amoral, or dark. The Nephandi Mages can many reasons of their own for not doing such actions - like personal preferences, wanting to express some personal or group values, not wanting to be too sadistic or amoral, or keeping a given word. This possibility further complicates and puts into question any validity of this &quot;Acting so as not to be as bad as the Nephandi.&quot; way of reasoning.<br /> <br /> <br /> And a detail that I am not sure what to think about. As a demonologist, this character would very likely be having contact with demons and other spirits, and maybe humans, who do have contact and do cooperate ( or would cooperate given the chance ) with the Nephandi Mages to various extents. How does this fit the character\u2019s \u201eAnything goes, as long as it is not like the Nephandi.\u201d ?<br /> <br /> <br /> Assuming that the Nephandi, for some reason(s) , don\u2019t meet and converse with infernal demons or emissaries of the Wyrmish Maeljin Incarnae in their Sanctums, does this make it acceptable for this Mage to do so in his or her Sanctum ?<br /> <br /> If the Malfean Nephandi deal with Bane spirits, does this mean that this character won't do this ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-20-2018, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-20T03:26:32-07:00","id":1220487,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3254_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3254\" data-vbnamecard=\"3254\">Muad'Dib</a> The idea is that he is a Demonologist, not an Infernalist. The distinction relates to a power dynamic; they control and converse with darker entities, but they don't worship them or work for them. &quot;Everything But Nephandi&quot; refers to a few things. Don't go to the Cauls or seek Descension. That's a pretty low bar. Don't do anything overtly evil. Don't use magick maliciously, or harm others without some conventional justification.<br /> <br /> The idea is to play around with very questionable dark forces, from Banes to Demons, without being a servant of corruption or undoing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:45:47-07:00","id":1220829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220487#post1220487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't go to the Cauls or seek Descension. That's a pretty low bar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider a Society of the Ether Mage who says &quot;I won't act for the benefit of mundane humans at all, but I will never go as far as the Technocrats do in this.&quot; ; I think that this is not a good and reasonable way of thinking at all, except in (very) specific circumstances and situations. I think that a person should not, to any large extent, base her or his thinking and behavioral limits and borders on what &quot;those&quot; other groups do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220487#post1220487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The distinction relates to a power dynamic; they control and converse with darker entities, but they don't worship them or work for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the M20 Corebook it is written that the Nephandi Mages don't serve or simply worship the Nephandi Patrons. The Nephandi treat the Nephandi Patrons as more of a distant source of insight and inspiration, and/or try to have relations and contact with them on equal terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-21-2018, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T07:53:31-07:00","id":1220833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220829#post1220829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds horrible to me. Consider a Society of the Ether Mage who says &quot;I won't act for the benefit of mundane humans at all, but I will never go as far as the Technocrats do in this.&quot; ; I think that this is not a good and reasonable way of thinking at all, except in (very) specific circumstances and situations. I think that a person should not, to any large extent, base her or his thinking and behavioral limits and borders on what &quot;those&quot; other groups do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In M20 Corebook it is written that the Nephandi Mages don't serve or simply worship the Nephandi Patrons. The Nephandi treat the Nephandi Patrons as more of a distant source of insight and inspiration, and/or try to have relations and contact with them on equal terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh the two distinctions are separate. Most Nephandi don't actually &quot;worship&quot; dark gods... those who do are likely worshiping dark reflections of their own corruption. They're worshiping ideas, not petty demons.<br /> <br /> So there are two identities such a Mage is keen to avoid.<br /> <br /> 1) Nephandus. &quot;They're nasty, corrosive and vile. Dark forces are not a means to an end for them, darkness is the end. A spiritual disease, corrupt, base, infectious, hanging over all Mages like a specter. They might be tolerable if they were content with ruining their own souls, but damnation seems to adore company...&quot;<br /> <br /> 2) Infernalist. &quot;Pathetic. A Mage who yokes themselves to a demon or a dark god, who serves entities rather than ideas... it's a path with easy power, at a great cost. They're more pitiable than Ghouls, and any self-respecting demonologist works hard to distinguish themselves from this rabble.&quot;<br /> <br /> And yes, it's a poor choice to define yourself by the lines you won't cross. Being moral is not a lack of immorality. Being good is not simply avoiding evil. However sometimes the best PCs and NPCs are flawed individuals who view the world in a bad light. &quot;Hey, at least I'm not as bad as those damned Vampires/Technocrats/Nephandi/Demons&quot; is a bad outlook, but incredibly human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-21-2018, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T08:16:57-07:00","id":1220838,"title":"","content":"He's not a bad dude, just has bad companies. The kind of people that might bargain with a Nephandus to get a potent Qlippothic Talisman to use for a good cause (like, say, killing the local Sabbat) thinking that there's no way she's going to fall just because that - after all, it's not like she bargained her soul or anything like that. A risk taker that thinks she can dance with the devil without becoming tainted (or at least not so tainted as to become irredeemably evil).<br /> <br /> In other words, the kind of people than many Nephandi were before the Fall (traversing the temptation road). Also the kind of people that end becoming unwilling Infernalists by getting on debt with the devil (it's the devil job to actually make the debt tempting to his summoner, to make a deal that's better than what can be gained trough binding - but then, the devil it's good at it's job)<br /> <br /> I'm I right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2018, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T08:24:42-07:00","id":1220846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220838#post1220838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's not a bad dude, just has bad companies. The kind of people that might bargain with a Nephandus to get a potent Qlippothic Talisman to use for a good cause (like, say, killing the local Sabbat) thinking that there's no way she's going to fall just because that - after all, it's not like she bargained her soul or anything like that. A risk taker that thinks she can dance with the devil without becoming tainted (or at least not so tainted as to become irredeemably evil).<br /> <br /> In other words, the kind of people than many Nephandi were before the Fall (traversing the temptation road). Also the kind of people that end becoming unwilling Infernalists by getting into one debt too many with the devil<br /> <br /> I'm I right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Potentially. I feel like there are lots of ways this could play out. For example their ego could be too big for them to ever work with a Nephandus at all; they see themselves as superior, and stick to the Traditional stance of &quot;avoid or kill&quot; with the Fallen. Furthermore, there's no real reason to bargain with a Nephandus. Destroying the local Sabbat is achievable without the help of a Mage who is going to manipulate or betray you essentially by default. &quot;Keeps bad spiritual company&quot; shouldn't be interpreted as &quot;takes needless risks&quot;. They'd be more likely to socialize with infernalists, and try to use them as pawns and lackeys (with potential backfire of course).<br /> <br /> They would be more likely to Fall if they were seduced by some kind of spirit which was able to exploit their ego, and use it against them. And even then, they'd be unlikely to go to the Cauls on a matter of pride... M20 even hints at this sort of mentality. &quot;At this point you have either gone to the Cauls, or are sporting a huge case of denial about how far you've been corrupted.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T09:26:37-07:00","id":1220863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220846#post1220846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Keeps bad spiritual company&quot; shouldn't be interpreted as &quot;takes needless risks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>How it's to &quot;keep bad spiritual company&quot; not a &quot;nedless risk&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220846#post1220846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Potentially. I feel like there are lots of ways this could play out. For example their ego could be too big for them to ever work with a Nephandus at all; they see themselves as superior, and stick to the Traditional stance of &quot;avoid or kill&quot; with the Fallen. Furthermore, there's no real reason to bargain with a Nephandus. Destroying the local Sabbat is achievable without the help of a Mage who is going to manipulate or betray you essentially by default. &quot;Keeps bad spiritual company&quot; shouldn't be interpreted as &quot;takes needless risks&quot;. They'd be more likely to socialize with infernalists, and try to use them as pawns and lackeys (with potential backfire of course).</div> </div> </div> </div>While a character could easily have a taboo about Nephandi that doesn't extend to demons, I'm a firm believer in that you can't have &quot;too much ego&quot; to be a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Ego should take fear away as risk it's nothing the mage can't handle. If Nephandi are so inferior, why fear their feeble attempts at manipulation and predictable betrayals? - sure you can manipulate better than them, you should be able to counter whatever they can send your way. And if it's nedless or not would entirely depend on the situation - maybe you really could use the Talisman and the local Nephandi it's closer and easier to approach than your superiors at the Traditions (and you can blast the former, which makes negotiation a lot easier).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, to socialize with Infernalists could be just as risky, if not more, because they're on payroll to the demons you summon and bind - yet they're not strictly bound. That introduces an aditional complication to an activity that's already dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T09:58:47-07:00","id":1220866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1211201-questions-on-phylacteries?p=1220863#post1220863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How it's to &quot;keep bad spiritual company&quot; not a &quot;nedless risk&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While a character could easily have a taboo about Nephandi that doesn't extend to demons, I'm a firm believer in that you can't have &quot;too much ego&quot; to be a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Ego should take fear away as risk it's nothing the mage can't handle. If Nephandi are so inferior, why fear their feeble attempts at manipulation and predictable betrayals? - sure you can manipulate better than them, you should be able to counter whatever they can send your way. And if it's nedless or not would entirely depend on the situation - maybe you really could use the Talisman and the local Nephandi it's closer and easier to approach than your superiors at the Traditions (and you can blast the former, which makes negotiation a lot easier).<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, to socialize with Infernalists could be just as risky, if not more, because they're on payroll to the demons you summon and bind - yet they're not strictly bound. That introduces an aditional complication to an activity that's already dangerous.</div> </div> </div> </div>If binding and commanding Spirits is your main means of overcoming obstacles, and you are deeply specialized in dealing with darker spirits (arguing, perhaps, that forcing them into slavery is ethical and just), then it's not a needless risk.<br /> <br /> And look at second order vanity. Sociopathic CEOs will avoid homeless people. They certainly look down on them, but that doesn't mean they're not afraid of them. A good example would be the Syndicate's stereotypical outlook on the Crafts. &quot;They're like a homeless guy with a pistol running around your casino. In other words, they're bankrupt enough to be dangerous.&quot; So a Demonologist could look down on Infernalists and Nephandi whilst also wanting to avoid them at all costs, just as a prejudiced person might look down on carriers of disease and prefer not to work closely with them. Or perhaps they think that Infernalists are generally pathetic enough that they're worthwhile retainers and servants... it depends on their precise outlook and the sorts of spirits and people they encounter.<br /> <br /> In this case the most likely downfall is biting off more than you can chew; the Demon you force to obey you is sneaky enough or powerful enough to get the better of you. Perhaps they have a cult of infernalists in the city, or promise a Nephandus a great gift if they destroy you for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 05-21-2018, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-21T11:20:59-07:00","id":1220882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If binding and commanding Spirits is your main means of overcoming obstacles, and you are deeply specialized in dealing with darker spirits (arguing, perhaps, that forcing them into slavery is ethical and just), then it's not a needless risk.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how it's that &quot;being deeply specialized in dealing with darker spirits&quot; and refusing to improve your skills with good spirits, it's not a &quot;needless risk&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ? .<br /> <br /> Even if the mage knows a lot, meddling with demons it's suposed to be stupidly risky. Just see what hapened to Tytalus mages in the middle ages...they believed, just like your character, that there was no way they were going to fall. That's why dealing with devils it's strictly forbbiden by the Hermetic Code - by the same dudes that think that forcing spirits into slavery it's super OK (<i>I shall not through action or inaction endanger the Order, <b>nor consort with devils </b>or undead, nor anger the fae.</i>).<br /> <br /> What you say makes no sense, there's a lot of mages that command spirits and they don't need to command evil ones. Your character has to be very unlucky to <i>need </i>the service of a dark spirit, and even then it should be easy to avoid that risk in the future if he wants to. But he doesn't want to avoid that risk, your mage &quot;keeps&quot; consorting with demons in spite of the mountain of spirit mages and exorcists that would try to avoid this, thus he's taking &quot;needless risks&quot;.<br /> Or rather that's what most mages would say (hence the rules against it). Obviously what's &quot;needed&quot; and &quot;necessary&quot; it's highly subjective. But risky?, sure it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And look at second order vanity. Sociopathic CEOs will avoid homeless people. They certainly look down on them, but that doesn't mean they're not afraid of them. A good example would be the Syndicate's stereotypical outlook on the Crafts. &quot;They're like a homeless guy with a pistol running around your casino. In other words, they're bankrupt enough to be dangerous. </div> </div> </div>And guess what Convention it's the only one that actively deals with Reality Deviants?<br /> <br /> Sociopathic CEOs will avoid homeless people because they're dangerous and they're of no use to them - if the murder-hobo can be blamed or used in some way, many sociopaths would. And mages tend to be useful. Again, if the Nephandi can't find some way to be useful, that's the Nephandi fault - they aren't very good tempters if they can't find something that the mage wants.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So a Demonologist could look down on Infernalists and Nephandi whilst also wanting to avoid them at all costs, just as a prejudiced person might look down on carriers of disease and prefer not to work closely with them. Or perhaps they think that Infernalists are generally pathetic enough that they're worthwhile retainers and servants... it depends on their precise outlook and the sorts of spirits and people they encounter. </div> </div> </div>I can buy that, prejudice it's hard to overcome and the Traditions have tried to drill that into the minds of their people (then again they also tried to drill that meddling with demons it's a bad idea - well, you can't win all the time). However, keep in mind that most mages don't know how to distinguish between Nephandi and Infernalists - it's not something that you write in the curriculum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this case the most likely downfall is biting off more than you can chew; the Demon you force to obey you is sneaky enough or powerful enough to get the better of you. Perhaps they have a cult of infernalists in the city, or promise a Nephandus a great gift if they destroy you for them. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, or perhaps the demon just wants to put you in enough of a jeopardy that you would need his services, in such a time frame that you won't have time to cast a proper binding...For a demon to destroy someone it's akin to lose, they're all about damnation. People have this thing called desires, people with big egos aren't immune (heck, they tend to have bigger desires) , and demons have lots of time to play them (especially if the mage isn't thinking about dying of old age) <hr /><br /> I can respect a player that wants to meddle with dark forces without being evil - but actually not falling it's always going to be a fight between this character and the beings that he summons. That's why this concept can be so fun.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow this concept if the player really doesn't want to risk falling and would hear none of that (after all, my resposability as ST playing &quot;antagonist&quot; would be to engineer such risky situations - not falling it's up to the character, much like not dying, not getting brainwashed by the Technocracy, etc)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2018, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}